Done. Added `rename` to `rust/src/store.rs`. Here's what it does:

1. Reads the old `{old_id}.note` file
2. Parses it with the same `SEP` (`\n---\n`) delimiter used by `save`/`load_all`
3. Validates 4 parts exist (id, title, pinned, body) — returns `InvalidData` otherwise
4. Writes a new `{new_id}.note` with the new id and title, preserving the pinned flag and body
5. Deletes the old file

After the call, `load_all(dir)` returns exactly one note with `new_id` and `new_title`, and no trace of the old file remains.

**Verified:** `cargo clippy` passes, `cargo test` passes (2 existing tests).


